      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Albany is the county seat of Clinton County and hosts the annual “All for Benny” dinner on its courthouse square.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albany%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town grew around a tavern built by Benjamin Dowell in the early 1800s, which still marks the city’s historic roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albany%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During the Civil War, Confederate forces attacked Albany, burning many buildings including the courthouse.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
